  "raw_text": "Pragyan Chemical Plant \u2014 Maintenance Work Orders\nSynthetic dataset generated for AI Knowledge Intelligence prototype. Equipment tags\nmatch the finalized P&ID set (PCP-PID-001 through PCP-PID-005). Note: formatting,\nnaming conventions, and completeness are deliberately inconsistent across entries to\nsimulate real-world messy maintenance records \u2014 this variation is intentional and useful\nfor testing entity extraction/resolution.\nWO-2024-0113\nDate: 14-Mar-2024 Equipment: R-201 (Reactor) Reported By: Ramesh Iyer, Shift Engineer\nSymptom: Jacket outlet temp reading 6\u00b0C higher than setpoint during batch 220. TIC-201\nloop appears sluggish to respond. Action Taken: Checked CV-201 actuator \u2014 found partial\nfouling on valve seat restricting cooling water flow. Cleaned and re-calibrated. Verified TIC-\n201 response time back to normal (<90 sec). Parts Used: Valve seat gasket kit (1x)\nTechnician: Suresh Patil Downtime: 2.5 hrs Status: Closed\nWO-2024-0114\nDate: 15-Mar-2024 Equipment: P-101 Reported: Feed Pump A tripping intermittently on\noverload during startup. Investigation/Action: Motor amp draw checked \u2014 within spec.\nSuspected worn impeller bearing causing increased load. Switched over to P-102 (standby)\nper XV-101/XV-102 changeover procedure. P-101 pulled for bearing inspection. Findings:\nBearing showed early-stage pitting, consistent with normal wear at ~14,000 operating\nhours. Parts Used: Bearing set (SKF 6205), lubricant Tech: S. Patil Downtime: 4 hrs (P-101\noffline, P-102 covering) Status: Closed\nWO-2024-0119\nDate: 22-Mar-2024 Equip Tag: PSV-201 Type: Scheduled Test Description: Annual pop-\ntest of reactor relief valve per OISD-STD-118 requirement. Result: Set pressure verified at\n8.4 bar (spec: 8.0-8.5 bar). PASS. Performed By: Vikram Singh (Safety Officer), witnessed\nby M. Joshi Next Due: Mar-2025\nWO-2024-0122\nDate: O2-Apr-2024 Equipment: C-301 / Distillation Column Complaint: Operators reported\nunstable overhead pressure, PIC-301 hunting. Root Cause Found: PV-301 control valve",
